  "body": "## octoscope 0.33.0\n\nTerminal dashboard for your GitHub account — see [README](https://github.com/gfazioli/octoscope#readme) for a tour.\n\n## Changelog\n### Features\n* 8d4365f5d32e51b1ac19d5735c29704f2c8fb55a: feat(scan): parse the npm lockfile's install-script surface (@gfazioli)\n* 9f51a20c4e6420966fdfd54e53b0294f0298b976: feat(scan): read the default branch's lockfile on a budget of its own (@gfazioli)\n* ce8e0479f54903d7e2f5db05b7b338b4d0203290: feat(scan): record the dependency install surface in the fingerprint (@gfazioli)\n* 53c0dcf9dcd16b25a48950138683e6eac649e466: feat(scan): say what the dependency surface did NOT cover (@gfazioli)\n* c94c34c8dab9b14530955980efbbc6b1a9022a81: feat(scan): the dependency install surface, diffed (@gfazioli)\n### Fixes\n* 9df575e921d2e87dd3503654d9cfeb7a9f7a4c19: fix(lockfile): an unmeasured schema, and a change that got lost (@gfazioli)\n* 523e2a5491214ae1578f4dc4cedab5253fe2dfe5: fix(scan): five holes in the dependency delta, one of them the verdict (@gfazioli)\n* 56003f178ee801d749e5820d12d6089d31c78e56: fix(scan): the lockfile precedence must hold when the file is unreadable (@gfazioli)\n* d2c0299d7ff3681ce125cdb1e5c9fb4feb875e2d: fix(test): format the scan helper the way go.mod's gofmt does (@gfazioli)\n### Other\n* 4014fdae9dcb55146c3d4fbb0075393e7543d5e4: chore(release): 0.33.0 — the part of a PR nobody reads line by line (@gfazioli)\n* d96b91035884eac7125ce2dba834104623e3640b: chore(release): refresh landing hero screenshot for v0.33.0 (@gfazioli)\n* f7024f89c198208b3efe9b5e68769eb054ea50e8: docs(scan): Axis 1b, and the measurements behind its weights (@gfazioli)\n\n## Install\n\nVia Homebrew (recommended):\n\n```bash\nbrew install gfazioli/tap/octoscope\n```\n\nOr download a platform-specific archive below and drop the binary on your `$PATH`.\n\nThe bare `*_<os>-<arch>` assets are the same binary without the archive, for a\n`curl` in a CI step or a Docker build stage:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL -o octoscope \\\n  https://github.com/gfazioli/octoscope/releases/download/v0.33.0/octoscope_0.33.0_linux-amd64 \\\n  && chmod +x octoscope\n```\n\n",
